# Copy to backend/.env and fill in:   cp .env.example backend/.env
# Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Only the backend reads secrets. The Vite frontend talks to the runtime
# through its /api proxy (or, for the Quickstart's own App.vue, directly at
# http://localhost:8200) and never sees a key.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model provider key. Read server-side by BuiltInAgent for its
# "openai:gpt-6-luna" model (the Quickstart's, unchanged). The Quickstart
# exports it in the shell instead; either works — `npm run dev` in backend/
# also loads backend/.env.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Runtime port. The Quickstart's server.ts reads PORT and defaults to 8200;
# frontend/vite.config.ts proxies /api to 8200, so change both together.
# PORT=8200

# CopilotKit Intelligence project key, for /api/copilotkit-threads only
# (Threads Drawer and Headless Threads), wired per the Vue Intelligence
# quickstart. Easiest: run the quickstart's CLI steps INSIDE backend/ — they
# write this variable to backend/.env, which `npm run dev` loads:
#   cd backend && npx copilotkit@latest login && npx copilotkit@latest project select
# Without it that runtime falls back to plain SSE (no thread store), because
# CopilotKitIntelligence throws at construction when the key is blank.
# Server-side only: never VITE_-prefixed.
# CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY=cpk-...

# The fixed local identity the Threads runtime assigns to every caller (the
# quickstart's "fixed identity ... for a local, single-user demo"; its value
# "local-user" comes from the quickstart's native examples). Change it to see a
# different, empty thread list. NOT authentication.
# APP_USER_ID=local-user

# MCP server for /generative-ui/mcp-apps. Defaults to the MCP Apps page's own
# HTTP example, http://localhost:3101/mcp, where `npm run mcp:apps` (backend/)
# starts the official ext-apps reference server.
# MCP_APPS_URL=http://localhost:3101/mcp

# Opt out of CopilotKit runtime telemetry (the runtime logs this on startup).
# COPILOTKIT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=true
